# November 21, 2026: western and northern Washington County, New York: Whitehall, Fort Ann, Kingsbury, Hudson Falls,
# Fort Edward, Argyle, Battenville, Easton and Salem. Drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny (region wash, 66
# places, most of them in Glens Falls, Hudson Falls, Fort Edward and along the old canal). This batch takes the
# Register listings and state markers the Atlas still lacked there: a canal-terminal museum, a 1913 firehouse moved by
# horses, two post offices with their New Deal murals, the county historical society's house, three old burying grounds,
# a stone arch bridge at a pre-Revolutionary mill site, the Fort Anne battle wayside, an old tavern at Battenville and
# two eighteenth-century brick houses. Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia read as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py),
# HMdb marker pages, Register nomination forms for the Whitehall Fire Station and the Moss Street Cemetery (NPGallery,
# text layer), the Washington County Historical Society's page for its house, the Skenesborough Museum friends' page,
# the Glens Falls Business Journal (2020) on the Anthony house, and OpenStreetMap for building points.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
def L(t,u): return [t,u]
def HM(n,t): return L('HMdb: '+t,'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=%d'%n)
def NR(ref,t): return L('National Register nomination: '+t,'https://npgallery.nps.gov/NRHP/GetAsset/NRHP/%s_text'%ref)
